<Solution>
  <Folder Name="/src/">
    <Project Path="src/Shenora.Core/Shenora.Core.csproj" />
    <Project Path="src/Shenora.Ipc/Shenora.Ipc.csproj" />
    <!-- The Android face of the mobile shell. In the gate deliberately (owner, 2026-08-02): a package
         no gate compiles is the objection this repo raises against every ungated artifact. The cost is
         real and documented in devtools/README.md — building this repo now needs the maui-android
         workload and a JDK (dev.mjs finds Android Studio's if JAVA_HOME is unset).

         Its peer `src/Shenora.iOS` is deliberately ABSENT from this solution: it can only be built on
         macOS, so listing it here would make `dev.mjs build` fail on the machine this repo is
         developed on. The two share every line of source (src/Shenora.Mobile/), so compiling one
         type-checks the other's content; what is NOT covered is its API baseline, which is gated in
         the macOS job instead. Said plainly rather than left as a gap someone discovers. -->
    <Project Path="src/Shenora.Android/Shenora.Android.csproj" />
    <Project Path="src/Shenora.Windows/Shenora.Windows.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <Folder Name="/tests/">
    <Project Path="tests/Shenora.Tests/Shenora.Tests.csproj" />
  </Folder>
  <!-- The samples ARE part of the gate: they are the reference composition and the e2e subject, so
       `dev.mjs build|verify` must compile them. This folder was EMPTY until P5.5 H5, which is how
       the sample could be red while `verify` reported green. Never packable (see their csproj). -->
  <Folder Name="/samples/">
    <Project Path="samples/Shenora.Sample.Desktop/Shenora.Sample.Desktop.csproj" />
    <!-- The D20 portability guard: plain net10.0, Core + Ipc only. It must be in the solution or the
         guard never runs (P5.5 H4.3). -->
    <Project Path="samples/Shenora.Sample.Logic/Shenora.Sample.Logic.csproj" />
    <!-- The MAUI head, hosting the SAME Shenora.Sample.Logic as the desktop sample. In the gate for
         the reason this folder exists at all: a sample outside it can be red while verify is green.
         It also turns D20's portability from a compile-time claim into two shells running one
         facade — and it is what proved the HybridWebView round trip on a device. -->
    <Project Path="samples/Shenora.Sample.Maui/Shenora.Sample.Maui.csproj" />
  </Folder>
</Solution>
